.TH LPCHECK 1 "2026-09-23" "learning-pi" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lpcheck \- run the pi learning-layer test suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lpcheck
.RI [ \-\-with-sidecars ]
.RI [ \-\-no-load ]
.RI [ \-\-sandbox " DIR" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lpcheck
is the short alias for
.IR ~/learning-pi/scripts/learn-check .
It runs the gate behavior suites, learning-layer resource checks, contract
coverage against
.IR contracts/learning-core.json ,
and an isolated, no-model load probe against a sandbox built from synthetic
state. It exits non-zero unless every invariant passes.
.PP
This is the same suite
.BR pisu (1)
runs before promoting an update. Run it directly to reproduce a diagnosis or to
check a hand-modified layer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-with-sidecars
Also run the learning-system
.I ops
unittest suite (read-only) against the real checkout.
.TP
.B \-\-no-load
Skip the load probe (used in CI, where no pi binary is present).
.TP
.B \-\-sandbox DIR
Run the load probe against a pre-built sandbox instead of building one.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every check passes, 1 otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pisu (1)
.PP
.I ~/learning-pi/CONTRACT.md
